# Alt 4 — Avatar-only, hover to expand

**Strip the footer to a single avatar.** At rest the bottom is just the user avatar — no name, no email, no org row. Hover reveals the full identity inline; click opens the combined menu. The leanest footer; reclaims the most vertical space for nav.

### Resting (one small avatar, left-aligned)

```
│  …nav…                        │
│                               │
├───────────────────────────────┤
│ (GD)                          │
└───────────────────────────────┘
```

### Hover (expands inline)

```
├───────────────────────────────┤
│ (GD) Greg Daniels · Acme  ⌄  │
└───────────────────────────────┘
```

### Clicked (combined menu)

```
   ╭─────────────────────────────╮
   │ ORGANIZATION                │
   │  ✓ Acme Inc                 │
   │    Globex Corp              │
   │  + New organization         │
   ├─────────────────────────────┤
   │  ⚙  Settings                │
   │  ↗  Sign out                │
   ╰─────────────────────────────╯
┌───────────────────────────────┐
│ (GD) Greg Daniels · Acme  ⌃  │
└───────────────────────────────┘
```

### Collapsed sidebar
Already an avatar — collapsed and expanded states are nearly identical, so the footer is visually stable across both.

```
│(GD)│
```

**Pros:** minimal chrome, maximum nav room, one resting target, identical in collapsed mode.
**Cons:** name/email/org hidden at rest (discoverability + multi-account clarity suffer); hover-only reveal is awkward on touch.
